      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "There is now an increasing awareness of the atherogenicity of the individual lipoprotein subfractions. In addition, the effects of commonly used antihypertensive drugs has been a cause for concern. Thiazides and loop diuretics both increase LDL cholesterol, but indapamide and spironolactone have no apparent effects. Beta-blocker monotherapy may also increase triglycerides whilst post-synaptic alpha-blockers do not affect, or slightly lower triglycerides, total cholesterol, LDL and VLDL levels."},
